astructure. Congress established the Federal Communications Commission to oversee spectrum allocation, not to pre-approve every radio broadcast, yet this proposed licensing regime treats frontier neural networks like forbidden nuclear material. Bureaucrats at the Bureau of Industry and Security lack the technical agility to evaluate dynamic training runs before compute clusters begin their work. When the state conditions innovation on prior administrative consent, it trades ephemeral safety theater for permanent economic stagnation. We must dismantle these proposed access barriers and unleash permissionless innovation across the entire technology ecosystem.",
